//// Front 20 F9 of 1.0.10-beta, decision 67 — `External`'s `inline` flag is
//// read by two emitters (erlang and beam, each over the annotation's last
//// argument), so `builtins.d.bp` declares it on `External.Erlang` and
//// `External.Beam` alone. On `Node`, `Wasm` and `Typescript` a written
//// `inline = true` is a switch nothing reads: before this cell it checked and
//// ran (exit 0), which is the configuration that looks like it bypasses the
//// dispatch table and does not. It is refused at the annotation, naming the
//// two variants that declare the flag.

#[@External.Node("Math.max($args)", inline = true)]
declare fn biggest(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32;

pub fn main() { @print(biggest(1, 2)); }
